IMPORT prelude

-- Part 1 of the Legislation Interpretation Act 2021 (South Australia): Preliminary.
-- Section 1 (short title) is machinery and has no rule.
-- Section 2 is not in the text (the Contents and the body number the first two sections 1 and 3).

§ `Part 1 -- Preliminary`

§§ `3 -- Application of Act`

DECLARE `What a provision of this Act is asked to apply to` IS ONE OF
    `this Act`
    `every other Act`
    `every legislative instrument`
    `something that is neither an Act nor a legislative instrument`

DECLARE `When an Act or legislative instrument was made` IS ONE OF
    `before the commencement of this Act`
    `after the commencement of this Act`

-- The application of this Act, or a provision of it, is subject to a contrary intention.
-- src:99 | (3) The application of this Act, or a provision of this Act, to an Act or a legislative instrument, or to a provision of an Act or a legislative instrument, is subject to a contrary intention.
@ref s 3(3) (src:99)
GIVEN `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the application of this Act is displaced by a contrary intention` MEANS
    `a contrary intention appears`

-- The provisions of this Act apply to this Act, to every other Act and to every legislative instrument,
-- subject to s 3(3).
-- The list does not say "only", so a thing that is none of the three is NOTHING.
-- src:94 | (1) Subject to subsection (3), the provisions of this Act apply—
-- src:95 | (a) to this Act; and
-- src:96 | (b) to every other Act; and
-- src:97 | (c) to every legislative instrument.
@ref s 3(1) (src:94-97)
GIVEN `what the provision is asked to apply to` IS A `What a provision of this Act is asked to apply to`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the provisions of this Act apply to` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `what the provision is asked to apply to` EQUALS `something that is neither an Act nor a legislative instrument` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the application of this Act is displaced by a contrary intention` `a contrary intention appears` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- This Act applies whether the Act or instrument was made before or after the commencement of this Act.
-- src:98 | (2) This Act applies to an Act or a legislative instrument whether made before or after the commencement of this Act.
@ref s 3(2) (src:98)
GIVEN `what the provision is asked to apply to` IS A `What a provision of this Act is asked to apply to`
      `when it was made` IS A `When an Act or legislative instrument was made`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`this Act applies to an Act or legislative instrument made at a time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `when it was made`
        WHEN `before the commencement of this Act` THEN `the provisions of this Act apply to` `what the provision is asked to apply to` `a contrary intention appears`
        WHEN `after the commencement of this Act` THEN `the provisions of this Act apply to` `what the provision is asked to apply to` `a contrary intention appears`

§§ `Tests`

#ASSERT `the provisions of this Act apply to` `this Act` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the provisions of this Act apply to` `every other Act` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the provisions of this Act apply to` `every legislative instrument` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the provisions of this Act apply to` `every other Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the provisions of this Act apply to` `every legislative instrument` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the provisions of this Act apply to` `this Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the provisions of this Act apply to` `something that is neither an Act nor a legislative instrument` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the provisions of this Act apply to` `something that is neither an Act nor a legislative instrument` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `this Act applies to an Act or legislative instrument made at a time` `every other Act` `before the commencement of this Act` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `this Act applies to an Act or legislative instrument made at a time` `every other Act` `after the commencement of this Act` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `this Act applies to an Act or legislative instrument made at a time` `every legislative instrument` `before the commencement of this Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the application of this Act is displaced by a contrary intention` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the application of this Act is displaced by a contrary intention` FALSE)
